{
  "format": 1,
  "name": "requests",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "HTTP for humans: GET/POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE over http and https, headers, query parameters, JSON, forms, auth and timeouts.",
  "authors": [
    "kurodaki-dev"
  ],
  "license": "Apache-2.0",
  "homepage": "https://github.com/kurodaki-dev/ton618",
  "keywords": [
    "http",
    "https",
    "web",
    "api",
    "client",
    "network"
  ],
  "requires": ">=1.0.0",
  "main": "requests.ton",
  "dependencies": {},
  "files": {
    "README.md": "# requests\n\nHTTP for humans in TON618 — `GET`, `POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH`, `DELETE` over **http and https**, with headers, query parameters, JSON, forms, authentication and timeouts. It needs `curl` on the machine (Windows 10+, macOS and most Linux have it; Termux: `pkg install curl`).\n\n```\nton618 install requests\n```\n\n```\nIMPORT://requests\n\nton.let r = requests.get(\"https://api.github.com/repos/kurodaki-dev/ton618\", {\"headers\": {\"Accept\": \"application/json\"}})\nif r.succeeded() {\n    print(r.json().stargazers_count)\n}\n\nton.let created = requests.post(\"https://httpbin.org/post\", {\"json\": {\"name\": \"ton\"}, \"timeout\": 10})\nprint(created.status, created.json().json.name)\n```\n\n## Calls\n\n`requests.get(url, [options])`, `.post`, `.put`, `.patch`, `.delete`, `.head`, and `requests.request(method, url, [options])`.\n\n| Option | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `headers` | dict of request headers |\n| `params` | dict added to the URL as a query string (encoded for you) |\n| `json` | any value, sent as JSON (`Content-Type: application/json`) |\n| `data` | a string as is, or a dict sent as a form (`application/x-www-form-urlencoded`) |\n| `auth` | `[\"user\", \"password\"]` — HTTP Basic |\n| `bearer` | a token — `Authorization: Bearer ...` |\n| `timeout` | seconds (default 30) |\n| `verify` | `false` skips the TLS certificate check (default `true`) |\n\n## The response\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| `r.status` | HTTP status code (`0` when no answer arrived) |\n| `r.text` | body as text |\n| `r.json()` | body parsed as JSON |\n| `r.headers` | dict of response headers, names in lower case |\n| `r.url` | final URL, after redirects |\n| `r.ok` | an answer arrived (even a 404) |\n| `r.succeeded()` | `ok` and status 200–299 |\n| `r.error` | why no answer arrived (network, TLS, timeout) |\n| `r.raise_for_status()` | throws on no answer or 4xx/5xx, returns `r` otherwise |\n\n`requests.quote(text)` and `requests.urlencode(dict)` are the URL-encoding helpers the module uses.\n\nNeeds ton618 1.0.0 or newer. It is built on `requests_send`, added to `ton.requests` in 1.0.0.\n",
    "requests.ton": "// requests.ton — a friendly HTTP client for TON618 (inspired by Python's requests).\n//\n//   IMPORT://requests\n//   ton.dict r = requests.get(\"https://api.github.com/zen\")\n//   print(r.status, r.text)\n//   ton.dict data = requests.post(\"https://httpbin.org/post\", {\"json\": {\"name\": \"ton\"}}).json()\n//\n// It runs on `requests_send` of ton.requests, which uses curl (so https:// works).\n// Only the names `requests` and `Response` are added to your script; the helpers\n// are prefixed with reqlib_.\nIMPORT://ton.requests\nIMPORT://ton.json\nIMPORT://ton.encoding\n\n// Percent-encodes a string for use in a URL (RFC 3986 \"unreserved\" characters stay).\nton.function reqlib_quote(s) {\n    ton.string keep = \"ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789-._~\"\n    ton.string out = \"\"\n    for ch in str(s) {\n        if keep.contains(ch) {\n            out = out + ch\n        } else {\n            out = out + \"%\" + upper(hex_encode(ch))\n        }\n    }\n    return out\n}\n\n// {\"a\": 1, \"b\": \"x y\"} -> \"a=1&b=x%20y\"\nton.function reqlib_encode(d) {\n    ton.array parts = []\n    for k in keys(d) {\n        push(parts, reqlib_quote(k) + \"=\" + reqlib_quote(d[k]))\n    }\n    return join(parts, \"&\")\n}\n\nton.class Response {\n    ton.function init(raw) {\n        self.ok = raw[\"ok\"]\n        self.status = raw[\"status\"]\n        self.text = raw[\"body\"]\n        self.headers = raw[\"headers\"]\n        self.url = raw[\"url\"]\n        self.error = raw[\"error\"]\n    }\n    // true for 2xx answers\n    ton.function succeeded() {\n        return self.ok and self.status >= 200 and self.status < 300\n    }\n    // The body parsed as JSON.\n    ton.function json() {\n        return json_parse(self.text)\n    }\n    // Throws when no answer arrived or the status is 4xx/5xx; returns the response otherwise.\n    ton.function raise_for_status() {\n        if !self.ok {\n            throw f\"request failed: {self.error}\"\n        }\n        if self.status >= 400 {\n            throw f\"HTTP {self.status} for {self.url}\"\n        }\n        return self\n    }\n    ton.function toString() {\n        return f\"<Response {self.status}>\"\n    }\n}\n\n// options: headers (dict), params (dict -> query string), json (any value),\n// data (string, or dict -> form), auth ([user, password]), bearer (token),\n// timeout (seconds, default 30), verify (false skips the TLS check)\nton.function reqlib_send(method, url, options) {\n    if options == nil {\n        options = {}\n    }\n    ton.dict headers = {\"Accept\": \"*/*\"}\n    if options.headers != nil {\n        for k in keys(options.headers) {\n            headers[k] = options.headers[k]\n        }\n    }\n    ton.string target = url\n    if options.params != nil and len(keys(options.params)) > 0 {\n        target = target + (target.contains(\"?\") ? \"&\" : \"?\") + reqlib_encode(options.params)\n    }\n    ton.let body = nil\n    if options.json != nil {\n        body = json_stringify(options.json)\n        headers[\"Content-Type\"] = \"application/json\"\n    } else if options.data != nil {\n        if type(options.data) == \"dict\" {\n            body = reqlib_encode(options.data)\n            headers[\"Content-Type\"] = \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\"\n        } else {\n            body = str(options.data)\n        }\n    }\n    if options.auth != nil {\n        headers[\"Authorization\"] = \"Basic \" + base64_encode(str(options.auth[0]) + \":\" + str(options.auth[1]))\n    }\n    if options.bearer != nil {\n        headers[\"Authorization\"] = \"Bearer \" + options.bearer\n    }\n    ton.let timeout = options.timeout == nil ? 30 : options.timeout\n    ton.bool verify = options.verify == nil ? true : options.verify\n    return Response(requests_send(upper(method), target, headers, body, timeout, verify))\n}\n\nton.dict requests = {\n    \"request\": (method, url, options = nil) => reqlib_send(method, url, options),\n    \"get\": (url, options = nil) => reqlib_send(\"GET\", url, options),\n    \"head\": (url, options = nil) => reqlib_send(\"HEAD\", url, options),\n    \"post\": (url, options = nil) => reqlib_send(\"POST\", url, options),\n    \"put\": (url, options = nil) => reqlib_send(\"PUT\", url, options),\n    \"patch\": (url, options = nil) => reqlib_send(\"PATCH\", url, options),\n    \"delete\": (url, options = nil) => reqlib_send(\"DELETE\", url, options),\n    \"quote\": (s) => reqlib_quote(s),\n    \"urlencode\": (d) => reqlib_encode(d)\n}\n"
  }
}
